<title>USA: TABLE - inTest Corp Q2 net $0.26/shr.</title>
<headline>TABLE - inTest Corp Q2 net $0.26/shr.</headline>
<dateline>CHERRY HILL, N.J. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				 6/30/97    6/30/96  6/30/97  6/30/96</p>
<p>			(000 omitted except for per share earnings)</p>
<p> Revenues		     $4,619     $5,043   $8,507  $11,132</p>
<p> Gross profit		  2,784	3,311    5,069    7,544</p>
<p> Operating income	    1,294	1,791    2,300    4,485</p>
<p> Net earnings		  1,042	1,435    1,887    3,692</p>
<p> Net earnings per share	.26	  .38	.48	.97</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding		 4,073	3,790    3,931    3,790</p>
<p>NOTE: inTest completed its initial public offering in June 1997.  The company said that prior to the offering, it had elected S-Corporation status and as a result did not accrue substantial domestic taxes.</p>
<p>Pro forma earnings adjusted to reflect operation as a C-Corporation for the quarter ended June 30, 1997, which would have been $739,000, or $0.18 per share, based on 4,073,317 average shares outstanding.</p>
